        }
      }
    },
    "Always stop to treat - don't try to treat while walking. This teaches the stop-and-reward pattern clearly." : {
      "comment" : "Tip for the \"Loose Leash Walking\" skill, emphasizing the importance of stopping to treat during walks.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "An operant (passive) skill where your puppy self-discovers that looking at you is rewarding. Creates deep, reliable attention." : {
      "comment" : "Description of the \"Looking at You\" skill.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
      "localizations" : {
        "nl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Een operante (passieve) vaardigheid waarbij je pup zelf ontdekt dat naar jou kijken belonend is. Creëert diepe, betrouwbare aandacht."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "As puppy eats the treat, step off again. Click for following, stop and treat. High frequency initially: every 1-2 steps." : {
      "comment" : "How-to step for \"Loose Leash Walking\" training, focusing on the frequency of clicks during training.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "As their head goes up, their bottom goes down" : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Wenn der Kopf hoch geht, geht das Hinterteil runter"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Cuando su cabeza sube, su trasero baja"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Quand sa tête monte, son arrière-train descend"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Quando la testa va su, il sedere va giù"
          }
        },
        "nl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Als zijn hoofd omhoog gaat, gaat zijn achterwerk omlaag"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "As they grab the treat, turn and run the opposite direction. This builds speed and enthusiasm - recall becomes a chase game they love." : {
      "comment" : "How-to step for the \"Come\" skill, focusing on building speed and enthusiasm for the recall.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
      "localizations" : {
        "nl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Als ze het snoepje pakken, draai om en ren de andere kant op. Dit bouwt snelheid en enthousiasme op - terugroepen wordt een achtervolgingsspel waar ze van houden."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "As your puppy's bottom touches the floor, you click THAT instant — not when they're halfway down, not when they've been sitting for a second. The click captures the exact moment. Then you have 1-2 seconds to deliver the treat. The click buys you that time." : {
      "comment" : "Example of using click timing to teach a behavior.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Ask for a down on the mat" : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
