    "Between 6-18 months, dogs commonly \"forget\" things they knew as puppies. This is biology, not failure! Stay patient and consistent." : {
      "comment" : "Tip for users about their dog's development, specifically focusing on the age range of 6-18 months.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Between sessions, watch for natural sits. When your puppy sits on their own, mark and reward immediately - this reinforces the behavior throughout the day." : {
      "comment" : "How-to step for reinforcing the \"sit\" behavior by rewarding your puppy when they sit on their own during training sessions.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
      "localizations" : {
        "nl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Let tussen de sessies door op natuurlijk zitten. Wanneer je pup uit zichzelf gaat zitten, markeer en beloon direct - dit versterkt het gedrag de hele dag door."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Build anticipation: puppy learns being at your left side predicts treats. Use visual markers (cones, sidewalk cracks) to remind yourself to click/treat." : {
      "comment" : "Training tip for building anticipation in Loose Leash Walking.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
