    "In classical conditioning, you actively guide your puppy into position using a food lure. This produces faster initial learning, making it great for physical positions like sit and down. The puppy follows the treat, and you reward when they reach the correct position." : {
      "comment" : "Explanation of classical conditioning, including the benefits and an example.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "In operant conditioning, you stay passive while your puppy self-discovers the desired behavior. When they do something right, you mark it with a click and reward. This creates deep, lasting learning because the puppy figured it out themselves." : {
      "comment" : "Text for the explanation of Operant Conditioning.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Inconsistent schedule (confuses the puppy)" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "nl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Wisselend schema (verwarrend voor de pup)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Increase reinforcement rate during this phase" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "nl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Verhoog beloningsfrequentie tijdens deze fase"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Instantly log a completed training session" : {
      "comment" : "Hint text for the 'Quick Done' button in the log sheet, explaining that it allows logging a training session as completed without needing to fill out all the details.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Integrate recall into daily life: call before meals, before going outside, randomly during play. Vary rewards - sometimes treats, sometimes play, sometimes just praise and release back to fun." : {
      "comment" : "Training skill content: how to integrate the \"come\" skill into daily life.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
      "localizations" : {
        "nl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Integreer terugroepen in het dagelijks leven: roep voor maaltijden, voor naar buiten gaan, willekeurig tijdens spelen. Varieer beloningen - soms snoepjes, soms spelen, soms alleen maar complimenten en terug naar het plezier."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "It happens" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
