    "Say 'sit' clearly in a normal voice, then immediately make the lure gesture. Mark and reward when they sit." : {
      "comment" : "How-to step for adding a verbal cue to the \"Sit\" skill.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
      "localizations" : {
        "nl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Zeg 'zit' duidelijk met een normale stem, maak dan direct het lokgebaar. Markeer en beloon wanneer ze zit."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Say cue, then step off with left foot. Always cue before movement begins - this becomes your walking command." : {
      "comment" : "How-to step for Training.Skills.looseLeashName, focusing on the importance of using a verbal cue before starting the walk.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Say puppy's name + 'come' in excited voice" : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Namen des Welpen + 'Hier' mit aufgeregter Stimme sagen"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Di el nombre del cachorro + 'ven' con voz emocionada"
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dites le nom du chiot + « viens » avec enthousiasme"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Dì il nome del cucciolo + 'vieni' con voce eccitata"
          }
        },
        "nl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Zeg de naam van je pup + 'kom' met een enthousiaste stem"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Say the cue word AS the behavior happens, not before. The dog learns to connect the word with the action." : {
      "comment" : "Description of the \"Word Must Match the Moment\" rule.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Say the cue word AS the behavior is happening, not before. Your dog learns to associate the word with the action." : {
      "comment" : "Training principle related to timing when saying the cue word during the training session.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Say the word only ONCE. Not 'sit, sit, SIT!' - that teaches them to wait until you sound angry. One cue, wait, then help with gesture if needed" : {
      "comment" : "Tip for the \"Sit\" skill, emphasizing the importance of saying the command word only once.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
      "localizations" : {
        "nl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Zeg het woord slechts ÉÉN keer. Niet 'zit, zit, ZIT!' - dat leert ze te wachten tot je boos klinkt. Eén commando, wacht, help dan met het gebaar indien nodig"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Say their name once in a happy voice" : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Den Namen einmal mit frohlicher Stimme sagen"
