    "Sit at puppy's level with clicker and treats ready. Hands behind your back - no lure, no gestures, no sounds. Wait." : {
      "comment" : "How-to step for the \"Watch Me\" skill: Sit at the puppy's level with a clicker and treats ready, without using a lure, gestures, or sounds. Wait.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
      "localizations" : {
        "nl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ga op het niveau van je pup zitten met klikker en snoepjes klaar. Handen achter je rug - geen lokmiddel, geen gebaren, geen geluiden. Wacht."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Sit down, spread arms, call with excitement" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "nl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ga zitten, spreid je armen, roep met enthousiasme"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Sit quietly with your hands behind your back. Don't call your puppy or make any sounds. Just wait. Eventually, they'll look at your face out of curiosity. The instant they make eye contact — click and treat! After several repetitions, they'll start offering eye contact more and more." : {
      "comment" : "Example text for the \"Teaching \\\"Watch Me\\\"\" concept sheet.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Sitting down with open arms is irresistible to dogs — it looks welcoming and non-threatening. This body language makes them want to run to you" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "nl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Op de grond zitten met open armen is onweerstaanbaar voor honden — het ziet er uitnodigend en niet-bedreigend uit. Deze lichaamstaal maakt dat ze naar je toe willen rennen"
          }
        }
      }
    },
